==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Blue-Eyed Asuka''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
One-Eyed Asuka is a very strong unit, boasting very high health and incredible DPS when taking into consideration her [[Surge Attack]]. She shares many similarities with [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]]. She has lower stats, [[Curse]] uptime, and her immunities are more situational, but just being a close copy makes her an incredible Uber to have. Against Colossal enemies, One-Eyed Asuka works very well if she outranges them, as her stats are higher against them, and she can briefly shut down their abilities. As one of the few units with [[EVA Angel Killer]], her performance against enemies from her [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Collaboration Event]] is superlative and renders the inflated stats of many EVA Angels moot.

A few minor differences between Kasli the Bane and Asuka are that Asuka has one less knockback, but 100 more Surge range. This means that Asuka has slightly less survivability than other Kasli variants but can sometimes pierce further into enemy lines. Her greater Surge range can also mean that the Surge sometimes doesn't hit the same enemies that her main attack hits, but both this and her one less knockback are pretty trivial and shouldn't be taken into consideration when choosing whether or not to bring her on a stage. Her lack of Wave and Surge immunity makes her vulnerable against units that rely on powerful waves such as [[Kory]], [[Berserkory]] and [[Elizabeth the LVIth]] as well as units that utilize surge attacks like [[Master Uril (Enemy)|Master Uril]]/[[Esoteric Uril (Enemy)|Esoteric Uril]], [[Kappy Jr.]]/[[Kappy Kawano]] and especially [[Malevolent Macho Leg Cat]] due to its Counter-surge ability.

Additionally, her [[Immune to Toxic|Immunity to Toxic]] and [[Immune to Freeze|Freeze]] give her viable matchups against [[Heavenly Herald Papuu]], [[Big Peng Z]], and [[Henry]] respectively.

